    {
      "question": "What to write on a move-in checklist?",
      "answer": "Write specific descriptions for every surface, appliance, and fixture across each room. Note exact flaws like scuffed baseboards, scratched flooring, or sticking cabinet doors. Record items that operate smoothly as good or working properly."
    },
    {
      "question": "Is a move-in checklist required?",
      "answer": "Some states require landlords to give tenants a written move-in condition checklist to claim deposit deductions later. Security deposit limits and inspection requirements differ by state law. You can check local statutes on the [HUD tenant rights page](https://www.hud.gov/topics/rental_assistance/tenantrights)."
    },
    {
      "question": "What should I check in an apartment before moving in?",
      "answer": "Check walls, floors, ceilings, doors, and windows in every room for physical damage. Test plumbing fixtures, kitchen appliances, electrical outlets, and heating or cooling systems. Confirm that smoke alarms and carbon monoxide alarms are present and functioning."
